WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.294 --> 00:00:05.534
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:14.822 --> 00:00:17.601
I'm starting to wish I hadn't
shot that security guard.

00:00:18.094 --> 00:00:22.317
His willingness to run in front of gunfire
would be real handy right about now.

00:00:22.317 --> 00:00:24.107
I'd tell him to run out there first,

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:25.259
I'd run the other way,

00:00:25.259 --> 00:00:26.418
it would be perfect.

00:00:26.418 --> 00:00:29.070
Teamwork: the ultimate sacrifice.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.594
Okay, time to go out in style.

00:00:30.594 --> 00:00:31.402
Zig-zag, zig-zag--

00:00:31.402 --> 00:00:33.161
[explosion]

00:00:33.161 --> 00:00:36.921
[panicking, explosions]

00:00:36.921 --> 00:00:38.037
[exhales]

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:39.639
Is he going to blow through the building?!

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.632
He doesn't have to!

00:00:40.632 --> 00:00:43.121
Personally, I would recommend he
NOT blow through the building!

00:00:43.121 --> 00:00:44.946
I shouldn't even suggest that to him.

00:00:44.946 --> 00:00:46.400
Why is this door not moving?!

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.524
It's blown off the hinges!

00:00:48.524 --> 00:00:50.504
I can see inside, for God's s...!

00:00:50.504 --> 00:00:52.500
THIS IS NOT LOCKED; THIS IS CHEATING!

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.989
TELL REALITY TO STOP CHEATING!

00:00:54.989 --> 00:00:57.240
Reality, how could you?

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.280
So, let's face the facts:

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.869
I don't have a grappling hook to
climb up the building,

00:01:01.869 --> 00:01:05.824
and this tank needs... seconds...
to turn the barrel left and right,

00:01:05.824 --> 00:01:09.084
so that's my window of really
shitty opportunity.

00:01:09.084 --> 00:01:10.061
Hey, I'm not here right now.

00:01:10.061 --> 00:01:10.754
This is my day off.

00:01:10.754 --> 00:01:11.116
So, don't--

00:01:11.116 --> 00:01:12.376
[explosion]

00:01:12.376 --> 00:01:13.000
No...!

00:01:14.465 --> 00:01:16.500
Okay, good, no second tank behind it.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:19.905
Oh yeah, what now, Captain Boom-a-lot?!

00:01:19.905 --> 00:01:23.467
How about you turn your gun towards me
and kill yourself shooting the wall?!

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:27.031
I'M RIGHT HERE, ASSHOLE!

00:01:27.031 --> 00:01:27.801
COME GET ME!

00:01:28.161 --> 00:01:29.822
THAT'S RIGHT, THIS SIDE!

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:30.876
Okay, bye!

00:01:30.876 --> 00:01:33.562
Doop-boop-doop-boodloodlood-doop, doop-boop,
boo-doo-boodloodlood, doop-boop, doopboopdoop...

00:01:33.562 --> 00:01:35.488
[missiles whistling]

00:01:35.488 --> 00:01:36.307
[explosions]

00:01:36.307 --> 00:01:36.801
[explosions]
Oh God!

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:38.568
[explosions]

00:01:38.568 --> 00:01:40.795
[explosions]
Don't be a nuke! Don't be a nuke!

00:01:40.795 --> 00:01:41.901
I-I can't handle a nuke!

00:01:43.249 --> 00:01:47.317
Okay, I'm not blind and my face is still on
my...face, so that probably wasn't a nuke.

00:01:47.317 --> 00:01:49.103
[gunshot]
WAAAAGH!

00:01:49.103 --> 00:01:51.378
LOOK OUT! THERE'S A SNIPER OUTSIDE!

00:01:51.378 --> 00:01:53.159
I SAID, LOOK OUT!

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:54.558
YOU NEED TO BE CAREFUL!

00:01:54.558 --> 00:01:56.667
WATCH OUT OR HE MIGHT SHOOT YOU!

00:01:57.346 --> 00:01:59.667
LISTEN TO ME, I SAID THERE'S A SNIPER!

00:02:00.712 --> 00:02:02.987
I tried to warn them.

00:02:02.987 --> 00:02:06.624
Actually, I thought that second guy was
going to run into his own grenade,

00:02:06.624 --> 00:02:09.118
but, I think he remembered about
it at the last minute.

00:02:09.118 --> 00:02:12.372
Some people are destined for a
special kind of greatness.

00:02:12.372 --> 00:02:14.590
[radio rapid beeping]
Jesus Christ, this thing is loud.

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.539
[radio rapid beeping]
I could hear it outside the building.

00:02:16.539 --> 00:02:18.831
[radio rapid beeping]
I'm going to turn it off.

00:02:18.831 --> 00:02:20.606
[radio rapid beeping]
Dammit, it's not...

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:22.801
[radio rapid beeping]
I hit the switch, what else am I supposed to do?

00:02:25.869 --> 00:02:27.467
I wouldn't make a good surgeon.

00:02:27.825 --> 00:02:30.757
Hey, I just realized, I don't know
how to fly a helicopter either.

00:02:30.757 --> 00:02:32.850
But, I think I should get a free pass on that one

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.000
because it's unreasonable to anticipate...

00:02:35.991 --> 00:02:39.680
Okay, I'm going to let you live
because I need you for an experiment

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.366
to ascertain whether tank shells
prefer blue or orange colors.

00:02:43.366 --> 00:02:45.578
GUARD: Sir.
Yes, that's good, you may call me "sir".

00:02:45.578 --> 00:02:47.962
GUARD: Okay, why not? Didn't
want to die alone anyway.

00:02:47.962 --> 00:02:48.729
Excellent.

00:02:48.729 --> 00:02:51.734
Okay chuckles, you wait there
while I figure out where we're going.

00:02:53.227 --> 00:02:54.095
Okay, is this...?

00:02:54.095 --> 00:02:54.704
[lock buzzes]

00:02:54.704 --> 00:02:55.775
No.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:57.298
[distant hivehand fire]

00:02:57.298 --> 00:02:58.919
Oh, you want to take a shot, huh?

00:02:58.919 --> 00:03:00.234
Hey, speaking of initiative,

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:05.231
I can't help but notice you were standing up
here while I was screaming for help downstairs.

00:03:05.231 --> 00:03:08.014
Some people might look poorly upon that.

00:03:08.014 --> 00:03:11.664
Oh wow, grenades. I could've
used these a few minutes ago.

00:03:11.664 --> 00:03:12.964
Guns!

00:03:12.964 --> 00:03:14.167
Shells!

00:03:16.044 --> 00:03:17.500
...more guns!

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.749
Holy crap, I've gotta find Eddie.

00:03:19.749 --> 00:03:24.223
If I can haul all of this stuff out of here
later, this is my ticket to a new life.

00:03:24.223 --> 00:03:27.575
Okay, I guess I can get this guard to
help me carry some of this stuff,

00:03:27.575 --> 00:03:29.663
but we should probably find a
way out of here first

00:03:29.663 --> 00:03:31.680
so we can come back here with a truck.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.668
GUARD: Yep, all that target
range time is gonna pay off today.

00:03:34.668 --> 00:03:39.812
Seriously, this might be a war zone,
but there is money to be made here!

00:03:39.812 --> 00:03:42.881
I don't know how many MP5s I've
seen just lying on the ground.

00:03:42.881 --> 00:03:44.734
We might need a couple trucks.

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:48.768
That guard knew the code to this place,
maybe he knows other stashes just like this.

00:03:48.768 --> 00:03:50.956
He might just tell us;
what does he have to lose?

00:03:50.956 --> 00:03:53.736
GUARD: I don't know if we should go
any further. Th-this doesn't look right.

00:03:53.736 --> 00:03:57.679
Eddie could interrogate him later if
he doesn't, but one step at a time here.

00:03:57.679 --> 00:03:59.523
I'll just take what I can handle for now.

00:03:59.523 --> 00:04:02.267
I'll be using some of this just
to get out of this madhouse.

00:04:02.974 --> 00:04:05.401
I don't have time to look
through all these crates now.

00:04:05.401 --> 00:04:08.939
If it's anything like these
shells, we're going to cash out.

00:04:08.939 --> 00:04:10.928
GUARD: Our luck has to change
sooner or later.

00:04:10.928 --> 00:04:12.259
It already has!

00:04:12.259 --> 00:04:13.556
Don't you understand that?

00:04:13.556 --> 00:04:16.684
Forget it, all I need from you
are the stash locations, okay?

00:04:16.684 --> 00:04:20.100
I'm not looking to split this share between
anyone else besides Eddie anyway.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.300
I wonder if Eddie can even
handle this much inventory.

00:04:24.066 --> 00:04:25.873
Fuck it, I know he'll try.

00:04:25.873 --> 00:04:29.996
I know Eddie. When I tell him about all I
found that's just lying here for the taking,

00:04:29.996 --> 00:04:32.237
he's going to get that sparkle in his eye.

00:04:32.237 --> 00:04:35.240
It's that same sparkle he had
before he going to Panama,

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.033
and I remember how that turned out.

00:04:37.878 --> 00:04:40.370
Oh-ho-ho! I have not forgotten you.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:41.534
I mean WE haven't.

00:04:44.746 --> 00:04:47.225
I'm not really the sentimental type, but--

00:04:47.225 --> 00:04:48.734
Well, no, I'm not.

00:04:50.273 --> 00:04:52.010
Okay, this must be the Sniper residence.

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:55.191
I received a bullet delivery from you
by mistake, so I'm returning it

00:04:55.191 --> 00:04:56.767
plus a little something extra
for your trouble.

00:04:59.641 --> 00:05:02.331
Okay, I'll mark down that you
received the shipment.

00:05:02.331 --> 00:05:04.209
Hey, you don't have a car, do you?

00:05:04.209 --> 00:05:07.091
That would make my life a lot
easier, you have no idea.

00:05:07.091 --> 00:05:09.103
But, you probably don't;
it got blown up...?

00:05:09.103 --> 00:05:11.268
GUARD: This place is a lot
bigger than I thought.

00:05:11.268 --> 00:05:13.531
Oh, so you don't know
where you parked it, huh?

00:05:13.531 --> 00:05:14.939
Well, I can't blame you.

00:05:14.939 --> 00:05:18.028
If I knew where I was going, a few
hundred people would be alive right now.

00:05:18.028 --> 00:05:19.408
But, they were all assholes, so...

00:05:19.408 --> 00:05:20.236
[lock jiggles]

00:05:20.236 --> 00:05:21.523
Yeah...

00:05:21.523 --> 00:05:23.119
So, what kind of car do you drive?

00:05:23.119 --> 00:05:27.007
I've been wanting to get a Crown Victoria
from a police auction for some time now.

00:05:27.007 --> 00:05:29.794
I thought it would be cool to drive it
around town with the police stripes,

00:05:29.794 --> 00:05:31.734
and splash some fake blood all over the hood.

00:05:32.229 --> 00:05:33.074
[metal grinding]

00:05:33.074 --> 00:05:34.908
Now, what is with these doors?

00:05:34.908 --> 00:05:35.716
WHOA!

00:05:35.716 --> 00:05:37.801
Don't turn into one of THOSE people, man.

00:05:38.748 --> 00:05:41.534
Okay, guess we're going here.

00:05:42.559 --> 00:05:44.165
Rrr...

00:05:44.165 --> 00:05:46.500
GUARD: I smell an ambush.
We'd better be careful.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:49.601
Hey, I'm the leader. I need you
to go find a camcorder.

00:05:50.874 --> 00:05:53.968
Then you can film me jumping around
here and climbing on things.

00:05:55.544 --> 00:05:59.328
If we're lucky, we'll catch some explosions
or jets flying in the background.

00:05:59.328 --> 00:06:02.067
Then I'll mix some music to it
later; it'll look sweet.

00:06:02.903 --> 00:06:04.510
Hey, you coming or what?

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:07.353
If he thinks I'm waiting on him,
he's in for a surprise.

00:06:07.353 --> 00:06:09.182
So, this must be where that bomb hit.

00:06:09.182 --> 00:06:11.270
Why did they bomb this? It looks empty.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.672
Did they miss?

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:14.133
Maybe they don't need a reason.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:15.901
Ohhh...

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:20.567
They'll never think to look up!

00:06:22.695 --> 00:06:26.234
Yeah, try and advance on me from
down there, surface-dwellers!

00:06:30.963 --> 00:06:34.100
Today's forecast is sunny mixed
with raining bullets.

00:06:34.685 --> 00:06:39.035
Huh, so was this building bombed
before or after there were troops inside it?

00:06:39.035 --> 00:06:39.634
Nee!

00:06:40.114 --> 00:06:41.794
I think it was after.

00:06:41.794 --> 00:06:44.077
Okay, how am I getting down?

00:06:44.077 --> 00:06:45.532
Uhhh...

00:06:45.532 --> 00:06:46.968
Oop-bop-paa!

00:06:47.591 --> 00:06:51.894
I've lost track of how many friendly-fire
incidents I've seen the military commit by now,

00:06:51.894 --> 00:06:54.292
but a friendly-bombing
is a new one on me.

00:06:54.292 --> 00:06:56.279
And those are just the ones I've seen.

00:06:56.279 --> 00:07:00.271
So, that means that the actual number
of friendly-fire incidents is a lot higher.

00:07:00.271 --> 00:07:01.467
Anyone here?

00:07:02.019 --> 00:07:03.000
No?

00:07:03.512 --> 00:07:05.391
So, what happened with that bomber pilot?

00:07:05.391 --> 00:07:08.849
Did he just sneak a flask of whiskey
up in the cockpit and take off?

00:07:08.849 --> 00:07:11.710
Maybe he decided to do a barrel
roll when he released the bombs

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:13.337
so they would fan out everywhere.

00:07:13.337 --> 00:07:15.565
And why shouldn't he if he's drunk?

00:07:15.565 --> 00:07:17.039
JESUS CHRIST!

00:07:17.039 --> 00:07:18.845
I almost shot you!

00:07:18.845 --> 00:07:20.322
And how'd that door open?

00:07:20.322 --> 00:07:22.487
Forget it; don't spook me like that!

00:07:22.487 --> 00:07:26.866
You're really making me think about bringing
back the Kill Everyone policy I had going on.

00:07:26.866 --> 00:07:27.534
Waah!

00:07:28.419 --> 00:07:29.367
[exhales]

00:07:31.388 --> 00:07:33.000
Okay...

00:07:33.641 --> 00:07:36.414
I think I know what we're going to do here.

00:07:36.414 --> 00:07:39.348
I mean, I think I know
what I'm going to do here.

00:07:39.348 --> 00:07:40.809
You just...

00:07:40.809 --> 00:07:43.251
GUARD: I'll be happy to survive
this with all my parts.

00:07:43.251 --> 00:07:44.534
Yeah, you do that.

00:07:45.442 --> 00:07:48.404
On a lighter note: I never told
you the second part of my plan.

00:07:48.404 --> 00:07:50.046
The cop car is just a beginning.

00:07:50.046 --> 00:07:51.202
The next part would take a while

00:07:51.202 --> 00:07:54.667
because I would have to pay somebody
to train a chimpanzee in hardcore karate

00:07:54.667 --> 00:07:56.300
and attack people on sight.

00:07:57.785 --> 00:08:00.759
I mean, he would have to be loyal
to me, of course--I'm the trainer--

00:08:00.759 --> 00:08:02.500
but everyone else would get a beat down.

00:08:03.658 --> 00:08:04.959
Then we could ride around at night

00:08:04.959 --> 00:08:07.105
and I could just let him loose
on the street for a while

00:08:07.105 --> 00:08:09.239
watching him beat the crap out of people.

00:08:09.239 --> 00:08:10.869
Nobody would be prepared for this.

00:08:10.869 --> 00:08:12.813
I could have a little whistle or
something I could blow

00:08:12.813 --> 00:08:14.441
[rumbling sound]
to get him to come back to the car.

00:08:14.441 --> 00:08:17.234
HELLO, THIS IS GROUND CONTROL.
PLEASE APPROACH MY SIGNAL.

00:08:22.053 --> 00:08:24.080
DO YOU SEE MY SIGNAL?

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.100
LET ME TRY ANOTHER ONE.

00:08:27.041 --> 00:08:29.067
HOW ABOUT NOW? DO YOU SEE THAT ONE?

00:08:29.909 --> 00:08:30.667
HELLO?

00:08:31.102 --> 00:08:36.000
NO, NO. PLEASE STAY INSIDE THE AIRCRAFT
UNTIL AFTER YOU'VE LANDED. THANK YOU.

00:08:38.559 --> 00:08:41.534
HOLD ON, WE'RE HAVING SOME TECHNICAL
DIFFICULTY. I'LL BE RIGHT WITH YOU.

00:08:42.022 --> 00:08:45.000
EXCUSE ME, SIRS? SIRS? YOU'RE
NOT ALLOWED BACK HERE.

00:08:46.524 --> 00:08:47.467
THANK YOU.

00:08:48.843 --> 00:08:50.968
OKAY, YOU'RE GOING TO HAVE TO
CHECK THESE THROUGH CUSTOMS.

00:08:51.385 --> 00:08:54.167
THIS IS GROUND CONTROL AGAIN.
YOU'RE FLYING SOUTH.

00:08:55.287 --> 00:08:56.701
FOLLOW MY SIGNAL.

00:08:58.794 --> 00:09:02.794
IF YOU DECIDE YOU WANT TO KEEP ON FLYING
TO ANOTHER AIRFIELD, THAT'S FINE BY ME.

00:09:02.794 --> 00:09:04.934
JUST KEEP GOING...somewhere.

00:09:05.531 --> 00:09:06.630
[metal grinding]

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:07.998
WE'RE GOING TO NEED MAINTENANCE DOWN HERE.

00:09:07.998 --> 00:09:10.150
WE'VE GOT A PROBLEM WITH THE HANGAR DOORS.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:11.634
OKAY, YOU'RE HEADING BACK EAST?

00:09:12.387 --> 00:09:15.534
AH, YOU'RE COMING AROUND.
OKAY, LET'S LINE IT UP THEN.

00:09:15.904 --> 00:09:18.367
YOUR APPROACH LOOKS GOOD
I'M JUST GOING TO GUIDE YOU IN.

00:09:18.744 --> 00:09:20.067
JUST FOLLOW MY SIGNAL.

00:09:22.154 --> 00:09:23.100
LOOKING GOOD!

00:09:29.078 --> 00:09:30.834
PERFECT!

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:36.029
Welcome to New Mexico. Ground temperatures
are 88 degrees with clear skies.

00:09:36.029 --> 00:09:37.834
Thank you for flying with us.

00:09:38.716 --> 00:09:41.601
Those aircraft didn't have the
best safety records anyway.

00:09:43.619 --> 00:09:46.955
I don't need to be checked by
Security; I work here? Thank you.

00:09:46.955 --> 00:09:47.434
[lock buzzes]

00:09:48.013 --> 00:09:50.500
Well, I don't want to go in
there anyway!

00:09:52.848 --> 00:09:55.467
Yep, have shotgun, will travel.

00:09:56.156 --> 00:09:56.943
One thing I don't--

00:09:56.943 --> 00:09:57.667
WAAH!

00:09:58.611 --> 00:09:59.167
Shit!

00:09:59.742 --> 00:10:01.561
Not again!

00:10:01.561 --> 00:10:02.795
Okay, walk away.

00:10:02.795 --> 00:10:05.052
I'm not getting involved
anymore than I am already.

00:10:05.052 --> 00:10:07.076
It's not like I can get
into any more trouble.

00:10:07.076 --> 00:10:09.334
What do I care? I launched a missile.

00:10:09.334 --> 00:10:11.498
Besides, I FUCKING TOLD HIM NOT TO DO THAT!

00:10:11.498 --> 00:10:13.329
So, what does he do? He does it again.

00:10:13.329 --> 00:10:15.534
That's the story of humanity right there.

00:10:18.525 --> 00:10:20.534
He didn't even find a camcorder.

